WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.100
Phineas and Ferb is now ten years old, meaning
that those of you who grew up watching it

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.880
are ready to enter the dating scene.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:11.220
So in the hopes of helping you find your own
true Isabella, it’s time to welcome you

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:18.019
back to MatPat’s Guide to Finding the One:
Animal Magnetism Magnif-inator Edition.

00:00:18.019 --> 00:00:20.740
“Hey baby, is there a magnet in your pants?

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:24.849
‘Cause my Magnetism Magnif-inator can’t
resist your buns of steel.”

00:00:24.849 --> 00:00:25.849
“Have you seen Perry?”

00:00:25.849 --> 00:00:28.109
“Is that the name of your platypus?”

00:00:28.109 --> 00:00:29.109
“No.”

00:00:29.109 --> 00:00:30.109
“Oh.

00:00:30.109 --> 00:00:31.109
Ooooh...”

00:00:31.109 --> 00:00:35.300
“Hey girl, has anyone ever told you that
you’re a Babe-inator with your settings

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.980
cranked up to STUNNING?”

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.280
“What’cha doin?”

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.140
“You.”

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:59.040
Hello, Internet.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:03.580
Welcome to Film Theory, the show that looks
at the animated characters who do crazy science

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.640
and does even crazier science off of their
work.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:10.380
Today, I'm returning to the world of Phineas
and Ferb, which we did an episode on a couple

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:11.380
months back.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:15.299
If you haven’t seen that one, definitely
check it out--we basically prove that Dr.

00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:19.929
Doofenshmirtz is secretly the good guy, a
sleeper agent for the OWCA.

00:01:19.929 --> 00:01:23.499
Episode is linked in the upper-right hand
corner if you’re SO EXCITED that you need

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:28.720
to watch it RIGHT NOW well you know where to find it...otherwise, just click
the link at the end.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:32.590
But even though that episode talked about
how ol’ Dr. Doof’s not such a bad guy

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:36.600
after all, it doesn’t mean he’s not without
a few flaws.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:42.179
Hey, we’ve all got our shortcomings...it
just so happens to be that Dr. Doofenshmirtz’s

00:01:42.179 --> 00:01:45.279
is literally his entire job.

00:01:45.279 --> 00:01:49.549
Starting from the very beginning, 
episode 1 of the series, we see how this so-called

00:01:49.549 --> 00:01:53.729
evil scientific genius basically doesn’t
even science, bro.

00:01:53.729 --> 00:01:58.569
This guy has hundreds of inventions over the
course of the series, but the Magnetism Magnif-inator

00:01:58.569 --> 00:02:03.849
from the pilot episode is not only the first
we see, but it’s also one that gets referenced

00:02:03.849 --> 00:02:06.140
time and again over the next four seasons.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:11.940
Quickly, we must separate the magnet from
the Magnifinator before it is too late...Is

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:14.660
it just me or is this a serious déjà vu
moment?

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.021
I feel like I've totally been here before."

00:02:16.021 --> 00:02:17.021
"That's it!

00:02:17.021 --> 00:02:22.280
Agent P, you've got to get to that time machine
and go back to the past, right before that

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:26.500
giant tin foil ball put you in a full body
cast for eighteen months."

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:31.060
Basically, the Magnetic Magnifinator is a
super-strong magnetic laser that somehow sucks

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:35.750
in a magnetic field on one end, amplifies
it on the other, AND manages to shoot it directly

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:39.500
at a target, which in this case is all the
skyscrapers on the Eastern Seaboard.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:45.020
Dr. Doof’s plan is to cover the Eastern
Seaboard in tinfoil, then use the Magnetism

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:48.460
Mangif-inator to pull on all the skyscrapers
on the East Coast so that everything on the

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:50.480
East is pulled toward the West.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:54.180
His goal is to ultimately wants
to reverse the rotation of the Earth.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:56.080
Why? Would you want to reverse the rotation of the earth?

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:57.620
...Well, that’s still up in the air.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:00.960
"You may ask yourself, why would he do this?

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:05.560
Well, let me just answer that question, I
haven't really worked on all the bugs yet.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:08.480
I mean, tin foil alone costs a lot."

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:13.460
But is Dr. Doof’s most infamous invention
of the series a scientific success or just

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.920
a load of electromagnetic excrement?

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:20.720
While it seems like this invention is a complete
disaster in every way, today’s episode actually

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:27.740
looks at the science behind the Magnetic Mafnifinator
to reveal just how advanced Doof is...and probably more accurately

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:32.580
how smart the creators of the show were in
designing this thing...and then I'll just talk about the critical

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.710
flaw that makes it all fall apart.

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:39.190
Get ready --today is going to be one polarizing episode.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.330
Polarizing episode.

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:41.330
Get it? Like Magnets?

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:47.300
Hey, I haven’t ever covered magnets, so
I’ve got a lot of pent up puns to unleash

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.800
So even though he doesn’t know WHY he’s
doing it, it’s clear Doof wants to reverse

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:52.010
the rotation of the Earth.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:55.960
But already there’s a huge problem with
that -- pretty much the first thing you learn

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.780
in physics: the concept of closed systems.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:03.240
Yeah, dust off like the first 10 pages of
your high school physics textbook for that

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.240
one.

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:07.800
In this case, the Eastern Seaboard that Doof
is shooting the Magnificator at and his own

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.310
headquarters are both part of what's called
a "closed system.”

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:15.690
According to classical physics, exerting a
force inside a closed system doesn’t change

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:18.340
anything about the system relative to its
surroundings.

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:22.770
In easier-to-understand terms, if Doof’s
goal is to change the rotation of the early

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:27.210
in space he’s never going to do that by
shooting one thing on the Earth at another

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:29.280
thing still on the Earth.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:32.870
Trying to do this would be like trying to
move a car by putting a moving tire inside

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.400
the vehicle -- nothing is going to change.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:40.290
The only way for a car to move is for it to
exert force against something external, like

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:41.290
the road.

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:44.920
By the same token, the only way to move an
object like the Earth through space is for

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:48.500
the object to exert a force against something
outside of itself.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:52.530
When you’re able to do that, it’s called
an OPEN system.

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:56.230
But in order for magnets to affect anything
about the Earth’s rotation, he’d need

00:04:56.230 --> 00:05:01.630
to be aiming the Magnifinator at the planet
next door, not some tin foil a few buildings

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:02.630
away.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:05.669
"As a lazy tailor would say, suit yourself!"

00:05:05.669 --> 00:05:09.520
But ok, so cat’s out of the bag that he
can’t change the rotation of the Earth.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:13.080
But maybe he could have done something else
interesting with the Magnifinator instead?

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:17.760
As it turns out, at the time of the premiere
episode of Phineas and Ferb, Dr. Doofenshmirtz

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:21.240
was actually eight years ahead of his time
with the Magnifinator.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:22.650
No joke!

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:27.020
Believe it or not, astrophysicists have spent
almost the last decade trying to catch up

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:30.150
to exactly what you see him doing in this
episode.

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:31.150
Think that’s nuts?

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:34.690
Let’s take a closer look at the Magnetic
Magnificator and see just what’s going on

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:35.690
here:

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:39.440
On the one end you have a huge magnet--seems
to make sense if you’re trying to suck the

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:43.380
buildings right off the pavement with magnetism,
but if you know something about magnetism

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:46.740
you’d immediately notice two huge problems
right off the bat.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:50.940
The first is that regular magnets don’t
have directionality.

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:53.670
They have poles, but that doesn’t make them
directional.

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:56.450
You can’t point a magnet like a gun and
go, “Bang!

00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:59.820
I just shot you really hard with this magnetic field!”

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:04.040
When you create a magnet, it honestly just
kind of sits there and emanates a magnetic

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:08.300
field all around itself...not exactly threatening.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:13.640
Problem two is that even if he has a strong
magnet over here, it won’t do anything to

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:16.020
those buildings over there.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:20.400
Magnetic strength works by the inverse cube
law, which means that as two magnetic objects

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:24.560
get farther away, their attraction drops off
exponentially.

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:29.480
An object that is twice as far away from a
magnet will require 8 times as much strength

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:30.760
to attract it.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:35.710
Increase the distance by ten times, and you'd
need to increase the strength by a THOUSAND

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:36.960
times to compensate.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:41.960
Dr. Doofenshmirtz is trying to use his magnet
to pull on buildings a kilometer away, which

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:45.199
is basically impossible for any magnet that
exists on Earth.

00:06:45.199 --> 00:06:51.800
The strongest magnet that currently exists in the world today is located
at the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory in Florida,

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:56.820
which has a magnetic strength of 25 Tesla
(that's the unit used to measure magnetic

00:06:56.820 --> 00:07:04.669
field and not,you know, the car) -- that's half a million times stronger
than the Earth’s own magnetic field, which

00:07:04.669 --> 00:07:09.500
seems ridiculously strong, but remember that
we as people living on the surface of the

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:13.820
Earth don’t even feel the Earth’s magnetic
fields and the only way we ever even notice

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:17.610
it is if we’re using an instrument sensitive
enough to detect it like a compass.

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:23.360
So to get around these problems Dr. Doof either
needs to focus that magnet or find a way to

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:26.740
get the magnetic field a heck of a lot closer
to those buildings.

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:32.080
And bizarrely enough, that’s exactly what we see him doing in the show.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:36.600
You heard that right, Dr. Doof is doing exactly
the right thing.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.430
"I did not expect that..."

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:42.560
Take a look at the other parts of the Maginifinator,
namely this tube here and what looks to be

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:46.449
a concentrated magnetic laser beam that he
shoots toward the city.

00:07:46.449 --> 00:07:51.479
He might not have known it at the time but
these are now real things that the most advanced

00:07:51.479 --> 00:07:54.590
physicists in the world are still developing.

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:59.110
The first is this magnetic pipe, or hose,
which is 100% a real thing.

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:04.180
By placing a magnetic field close to the opening
of a specialized tube, theoretical physicists,

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:08.260
or just “Theorists” as I like to call
them, have actually managed to preserve a

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:12.630
magnetic field over much longer distances
than the field would exist by itself.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:17.780
Right now they believe they could actually
preserve 90% of a magnetic field in a magnetic

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:23.960
superconductor hose, transporting magnetism
in a way that previously seemed impossible.

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:27.740
The other thing that’s going on here is
potentially even more exciting because it

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:33.919
doesn’t just involve magnets, it involves
lasers, which are just inherently cool.

00:08:33.919 --> 00:08:37.990
We can see that the Magnifinator doesn’t
just seem to be a plain old magnetic field

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:40.979
generator, it’s a laser beam at one end.

00:08:40.979 --> 00:08:45.140
Once again, Dr. Doof is actually way ahead
of his time, creating what would have been

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:53.500
the world’s first super magnet laser, something
that, as of 2016, is being built for the first time ever.

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:57.920
These magnet lasers are pretty much exactly
what they sound like: ultra powerful lasers

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:03.210
that have the special ability of also creating
extremely powerful magnetic fields--thousands

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:07.400
of times more powerful than any field humans
have created in the past.

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:10.420
Basically these thing would be a lot like Metroid grapple beam.

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:14.300
The physics behind these things is incredibly
complicated and if you’re a Faraday Effect

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:18.190
aficionado I invite you to dive into these
things in the comments, but for what we’re

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:22.050
talking about right now I’m basically going
to boil it up to the very top level.

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:26.920
Lasers--which are basically streams of super-energized
electrons--start to get all kinds of special

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:29.640
properties as you turn up the intensity of
the laser.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:34.680
One of the special properties that starts
to happen is radiation friction, or RF.

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:39.950
This is basically the friction of electrons
at incredibly high energy levels, which gives

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:45.560
you more than just atomic rug burn, it actually
creates an ultra-powerful magnetic field around

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:46.560
the laser beam.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:50.580
Again, this is the made-for-Youtube version
of this incredibly advanced science, so if

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:54.890
this sounds interesting to you, have a look
at this stuff, it’s literally as close as

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:57.340
humans get to magic.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:10:00.500
Anyway, what you come out of this process
with is a magnetic field on the order of 1

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:03.950
Billion Gausse, which is a big number but
doesn’t mean a lot if we don’t have anything

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:04.950
to compare it to.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:09.740
So for comparison, an MRI machine creates
a magnetic field of 70 thousand Gausse, which

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:13.310
is enough to interfere with pacemakers, metal
prosthetics, or any other electronics that

00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:14.320
end up inside it.

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:19.310
And this magnetic field is in the billions
of Gausse, basically an astronomic level,

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:27.120
and can do things like contain nuclear fusion
and rival the magnetic strength of a neutron

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:28.120
star.

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:32.710
You heard that right, Doof created a device
that rivals the power of STARS!

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:37.380
So yeah, with that kind of magnetism, Dr.
Doofenshmirtz could definitely do some serious

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:38.240
damage.

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:44.900
"If you give me another chance I promise to hurt you in the right way, with
cartoonish physical violence and elaborate

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:48.620
traps made out of strange things I bought
over the internet."

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:52.420
OK, so far we’ve found a way to make the
Magnifinator possible, in theory.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:57.520
But here’s where it all comes undone: To
create what he thinks will be a super strong

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:02.451
magnetic attraction, Dr. Doofenshmirtz covers
all the skyscrapers on the Eastern seaboard

00:11:02.451 --> 00:11:03.451
with tin foil.

00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:06.880
Let’s see what happens at the big moment
when he’s going to rip them all up!

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:12.480
"Pull the Eastern Seaboard thereby reversing rotation of the -

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.800
“Oh, well that didn’t work.”

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.660
You bet it didn’t my little Doofle-pants.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:23.540
Get your dipoles straight, my friend, you
created the world’s first magnetic hose,

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:28.270
hooked up to the world’s most advanced magnetic
laser in history which can literally harness

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:35.399
the power of effing STARS, but you forgot
one thing...one CRUCIAL detail in your ENTIRE plot.

00:11:35.399 --> 00:11:36.790
Tin foil isn’t magnetic.

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:40.990
While it's true that metals like iron, nickel,
and cobalt are attracted to magnets, not all

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:42.850
metals are.

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:46.170
Ferromagnetism is the property that we use
to describe things that are magnetic.

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:53.200
What we refer to as "tin foil" isn't magnetic
and...isn’t actually made of tin, at least

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:54.200
not today.

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:58.370
Back in the 1800's, actual tin foil sheets
were commonly used, but when it came to covering

00:11:58.370 --> 00:12:02.080
food, they left everything they covered with
a metallic flavor, which is why in the 1930s

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:06.680
and 40’s tin was replaced with cheaper,
tastier aluminum.

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:10.730
But while switching to aluminum may help Doof’s
tuna sandwich stay fresher, it’s not going

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:16.870
to help him create mega-magnets any sooner,
since neither tin nor aluminum are magnetic.

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:20.680
In fact if anything, covering these buildings
in foil is going to make it harder for the

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:24.370
pieces of these buildings that ARE magnetic,
like all the steel, iron supports, or pipes,

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:25.560
to all come ripping out.

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:29.170
He’s literally creating a barrier against
his own magnet laser.

00:12:29.170 --> 00:12:34.800
And yes, technically iron foil does exist
and would be magnetic here, but Dr. Doof specifically

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:39.500
says he uses tin foil because “I mean, tin
foil alone costs a lot."

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:43.820
If he were to upgrade to iron foil, to cover
even the one city section we see on screen

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:48.760
in the episode, which is just a tiny fraction
of the real Eastern seaboard, it would cost

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:55.440
at least $742,500 and we know realistically
that for the entire East Coast he’d have

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:58.540
to repeat this dozens or hundreds of different times.

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:03.740
So in the end, despite all the resources and
incredibly advanced technology Dr. Doofenshmirtz

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:08.970
has at his fingertips, from ultra lasers to
theoretical physics, his whole plan is undone

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:16.040
by not paying attention to the most fundamental
rules of magnetism. The stuff that we learn in like third grade!

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:20.370
And instead of taking over the world in the
very first episode, we got four more seasons

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:22.950
of Phineas and Ferb science to dissect.

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:27.700
So don’t worry, we’ll have plenty more of
his plans to FOIL over on this channel, so make sure

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:32.480
you activate the SUBSCRIBE-INATOR you see
on screen right now so you’re around as

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:37.709
we cover more classic Disney Channel and Nickelodeon
shows, everything from Danny Phantom and Fairly

00:13:37.709 --> 00:13:40.500
Oddparents to Drake and Josh and Zach and
Cody.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:46.260
Here’s our previous Phineas and Ferb episode on the left
and remember, that’s just a Theory.

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:47.340
A Film Theory!

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:49.340
AAAAAAAAAND -

